WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.100
It's the biggest cinematic event in years,
and Avengers: Infinity War doesn't disappoint,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.920
shocking fans with all sorts of stuff that
we're totally about to spoil.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.720
Seriously, this video is full of spoilers.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.889
What kind of spoilers?

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:17.429
Well, like this spoiler: at the end of Infinity
War, half the universe was wiped out with

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:22.380
a single snap of Thanos's giant purple hot
dog fingers.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.279
But considering the deaths were supposedly
random, fans couldn't help but notice that

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:29.359
all of the founding Avengers somehow survived.

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.480
So why did these specific characters gain
plot immunity?

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.840
Here's a look at the real reasons these Avengers
survived Infinity War.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.410
Bringing the series full circle

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.660
2012's The Avengers brought the Marvel Cinematic
Universe together for the first time, weaving

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.290
together heroes from separate franchises into
one blockbuster behemoth that changed the

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.610
face of cinema.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.370
Plus, it also introduced the threat of Thanos
in a key mid-credit scene teaser.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.090
So it's only fitting that 2019's Avengers
4 will bring the franchise full circle with

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:02.940
the original team re-assembling to save the
universe one last time.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.340
It's no coincidence that Captain America,
Iron Man, Thor, Hulk, and Black Widow all

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.100
survived Thanos's finger snap.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.369
And though Hawkeye was missing from Infinity
War, it's already been confirmed that Jeremy

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:15.549
Renner will be in Avengers 4.

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:19.649
It all began with these six Avengers, and
it looks like it's probably going to end with

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:21.240
them as well.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.899
The last hurrah

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:26.850
Though the details of their contracts aren't
made public, comments from stars like Robert

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.799
Downey Jr. and Chris Evans have hinted at
the fact that many of the key players in the

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:35.310
MCU are apparently nearing the ends of their
contracts and they may not be back.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:39.749
Though Chris Hemsworth has indicated he might
be up for another Thor film, Evans has been

00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:42.350
pretty clear that he's ready to move on to
something else.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.609
"A lot of our contracts are through.

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:46.380
I mean, myself, Downey, Hemsworth.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.909
We all kinda started roughly at the same time.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:52.829
And I think we all through Avengers 4 kinda
wraps it up."

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:57.270
With Captain America and possibly Iron Man
set to depart the series for good, it makes

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.330
sense for them to be the heart of Avengers
4 just as they've been the heart of the MCU

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.060
for the past 10 years.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.049
One or both of them may even sacrifice himself
to set the universe right.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:11.310
Cap's story is about always doing what's right
no matter how hard it gets, while Iron Man's

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.390
arc is about a selfish man learning to be
selfless, so putting it all on the line would

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:19.360
make perfect sense for either or both of them.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.140
Iron Man's destiny

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:28.030
In Infinity War, Doctor Strange uses the Time
Stone to look at 14,000,605 possible futures,

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.430
and finds only one in which the heroes manage
to defeat Thanos.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:36.110
Later, when Thanos is about to kill Tony Stark,
Strange gives him the Time Stone in return

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.390
for Tony's life, telling Tony, "It's the only
way."

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.920
It's clear that Iron Man is key to whatever
secret plan Dr. Strange has formulated.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.620
Which makes sense, as Stark's character arc
for the past several years has been all about

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.180
dealing with the threat of alien invasion,
and Thanos in particular.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.870
Thematically, Tony has to be there at the
end to take down Thanos, something that Dr.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.430
Strange apparently knows as well.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:02:59.430
The Hulk's return

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:04.900
Remember, Bruce Banner never turned into the
Hulk in Infinity War's final battle.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.810
We were all waiting for those green muscles
to erupt out of the Hulkbuster armor, but

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.230
the moment never came.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:15.290
Hulk refusing to come out of Banner's subconscious
is almost unprecedented and the implication

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.840
is that he was traumatized by his encounter
with Thanos.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.950
Banner's inability to transform is a setup
building to the dramatic reappearance of the

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:27.530
Hulk at the exact moment when his strength
is most needed, which is bound to be in Avengers

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.790
4.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.810
Captain America's final stand

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.880
One of the most iconic moments in the original
Infinity Gauntlet comic book is when Captain

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.410
America, just a regular guy from Brooklyn,
stands up to Thanos, a death god with power

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.380
of reality itself.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.150
Cap knows he can't win, but he stands against
Thanos anyway because it's the right thing

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.150
to do.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.220
"You just don't know when to give up, do you?"

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.480
"I can do this all day."

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.260
It's one of the most iconic Captain America
moments of all time, and while it's briefly

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.950
alluded to in Infinity War, it would be a
real shame if we didn't get to see the whole

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.340
showdown in Avengers 4.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.069
Black Widow's redemption

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:09.069
Much of Natasha Romanoff's MCU backstory remains
a mystery, but we know she's trying to atone

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:10.740
for the sins of her past.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:11.840
As she put it in Avengers,

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.200
"I've got red in my ledger.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.620
I'd like to wipe it out."

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.680
What that means, is that she owes the world
a debt for the evil things she's done, necessitating

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.990
the heroic choices she now makes.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.940
Saving half the living beings in the entire
universe would be the ultimate way to settle

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.500
those debts once and for all.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.400
War Machine's connections

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.190
Of the official Avengers who survived the
finger snap, War Machine is the only non-founding

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.190
member.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.380
So why is he still around?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.560
Well, besides being one of the earliest heroes
in the MCU, he's also a key government liaison.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.160
Sure, he disobeyed orders by not arresting
Cap's team when they came to him for help

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.430
in Infinity War, but with his military and
political experience, he can probably smooth

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:58.410
it over and get the Avengers the kind of help
they'll need now that Nick Fury and the remaining

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.770
SHIELD hierarchy have been turned to dust.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.240
Rocket's family

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.460
One of the most shocking things about the
end of Infinity War is that all of the Guardians

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.060
of the Galaxy die.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.880
All of them, that is, except Rocket.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.880
And it makes sense.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.370
Up until now, Rocket's story up to this point
has been about his adopted family teaching

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.560
him to be less cynical and selfish.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.570
With that family gone, it's up to Rocket to
put those lessons into play and do the right

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:27.310
thing without prompting from Star-Lord or
Groot, but because he's now a hero himself

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.310
in his own right.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:32.930
Plus, he's also the only space pilot the Avengers
have, and if they're going to track down Thanos,

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.990
that could be a really handy skill.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.340
Nebula's revenge

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:42.340
Before Infinity War, Nebula wanted to kill
her adopted father Thanos, and that was before

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.000
he tortured her, murdered her sister, and
wiped out half the universe.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.760
Yet, Nebula still lives, and we have good
reason to believe she may get the revenge

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.960
she seeks.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.980
Because in the comics, it's not the combined
might of Earth's Mightiest Heroes that defeats

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:58.449
Thanos and restores life to those he murdered,
it's Nebula!

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:03.060
Yep, in the original story, Nebula steals
the Infinity Gauntlet from Thanos and uses

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.949
its power to return the universe to its original
state, bringing untold trillions of people

00:06:07.949 --> 00:06:09.860
back to life around the universe.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:14.271
She may not be an official member of the Guardians
of the Galaxy or the Avengers, but before

00:06:14.271 --> 00:06:19.300
all is said and done, it may be Nebula who
finally gets the last laugh on dear old dad.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.990
"I will buy a warship with every conceivable
instrument of death.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:26.620
I will hunt my father like a dog and I will
tear him apart, slowly."

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.620
Thanks for watching!

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.300
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.650
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

